# README - AVL Tree

## Aim
This folder demonstrates insertion into an AVL tree and the balancing rotations that keep the tree height-balanced.

---

## Algorithm
1. Insert each value using the binary-search-tree ordering rule.
2. Update the height of each ancestor after insertion.
3. Calculate each node's balance factor from its left and right subtree heights.
4. Apply a single or double rotation when a node becomes unbalanced.
5. Print preorder and inorder traversals, followed by the tree height.

---

## How it works
An AVL tree is a binary search tree in which the heights of a node's left and right subtrees differ by at most one. The program handles the four imbalance cases (left-left, left-right, right-right, and right-left) with rotations. Duplicate values are ignored.

---

## Functionality
- Insert values while maintaining AVL balance
- Display preorder and inorder traversals
- Report the tree height

---

## Time and Space Complexity
- Insert: O(log n)
- Preorder / inorder traversal: O(n)
- Extra space: O(n) for tree nodes; O(log n) recursion stack for insertion and traversal
